<urn:atm:triage:finding/SMK-004>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "SMK-004" ;
  triage:title "Task-start receipt to the assigner renders through the Task nudge template with assignee-style ack/execute instructions" ;
  triage:description "fenix (ATM 01M2B4CC8CHFPPR7DR5CYSTV3E, 2026-09-12T15:39:37Z), found investigating Rand's live nudge-test-1/2/3 exercise against cipher (2026-09-12T15:27-15:30Z, on the 1.5.16 prerelease). Not a bug: the apparent 'rogue' re-delivery of the nudge-test-2 task_started message to team-lead is the correct NudgeMode::Deferred receipt sent to the assigner (herdr_task_start.rs:53-68) -- it is written onto the task's `started` event at the instant the assignee is nudged, but its delivery to the assigner is deferred until the assigner goes idle, so it can arrive well after the fact and read as a surprise repeat. Sequencing verified clean across all three tasks (one head-nudged-at-a-time, no duplicate receipts). The minor wording defect: because the receipt carries a task_id, it renders through BuiltInNudgeTemplateKind::Task (nudge_template.rs:91), which is written for an actual task assignment -- so the assigner is told \"ack the message\" and \"execute the assigned task\" for a task that is not theirs to execute, and the underlying WriteRequest sets requires_ack=false, making the ack instruction actively wrong. Suggested fix: a receipt-specific built-in nudge kind (read + <task id> + description, no ack/execute action lines). fenix's estimate: cipher-sized fix, pending Rand's go-ahead." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-ba" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:category "code-quality" ;
  triage:severity "minor" ;
  triage:source "qa" ;
  triage:repeatable true ;
  triage:sweepScope "crates/atm-http-runtime/src/herdr_task_start.rs" ;
  triage:status "open" ;
  triage:dispatchReady false ;
  triage:triagedAt "2026-09-12T15:39:37Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:deferredNote "Not a product defect in delivery correctness -- confirmed working as designed (deferred receipt semantics). Wording-only fix; dispatchReady left false pending Rand's go-ahead per fenix's note. fenix (ATM 01M2B4STTJ43RE7XY9WA1FRHM4, 2026-09-12T15:46:58Z), root-cause follow-up with Rand's exact timing (rogue nudge arrived >=1 min after all three closes): the BA.5 queue-item rule, not a defect -- the task_started receipt (NudgeMode::Deferred) is an open queue item while unread, and each successful handoff re-arms nudge_pending_at = now + 60s (TASK_REMINDER_INTERVAL_MS); the pump re-prompts once per interval while the item stays open. mail_message_states confirms: receipt-1 read at 15:27:59 (25s, no re-prompt needed); receipt-2 (written 15:29:39) not read until 15:32:03 -- team-lead read receipt-3 and close-3 first at 15:31:11 -- so receipt-2 was re-prompted at the next idle tick after its 60s re-arm. The close-2 report (an immediate send, not a deferred marker) sat unread until 15:34:40 and was never re-nudged, confirming only deferred items re-prompt. So SMK-004 is two compounding wording/design issues on the same receipt: (a) Task-template ack/execute wording is wrong for a receipt, and (b) the receipt re-prompts every 60s until read, which amplifies (a)'s confusion each time it re-fires. Rand is opening a broader nudge-granularity design discussion; the fix shape (receipt-specific nudge kind, and whether receipts should be deferred/re-prompted at all) will come out of that. Keep dispatchReady false and #1431 held pending that discussion." ;
  triage:foundIn triage:BA6 ;
  triage:foundAt "2026-09-12T15:39:37Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/SMK-004/1> ;
  triage:triageRecordVersion "2" .

<urn:atm:triage:occurrence/SMK-004/1>
  a triage:Occurrence ;
  triage:file "crates/atm-http-runtime/src/nudge_template.rs" ;
  triage:line 91 ;
  triage:snippet "BuiltInNudgeTemplateKind::Task renders \"ack the message\" / \"execute the assigned task\" for an assigner's task-start receipt (herdr_task_start.rs:53-68, NudgeMode::Deferred), which is not an assignment and has requires_ack=false on its WriteRequest -- instructions are misleading for the receiving assigner" ;
  triage:status "open" ;
  triage:closed false ;
  triage:branch "develop" ;
  triage:headSha "11b6fcf0f" ;
  triage:occursIn <urn:atm:triage:worktree/SMK-004/1> .

